 "notes": "Spine: need -> hypothesis -> WO2 base + M sweep -> DFT: W-M bond weakening (F1b-d) -> dG_H* volcano (F1e) -> down-select Ni -> hydrothermal NWs -> reductive anneal -> single-phase Ni-WO2 -> oxidised W (XANES) -> longer, charge-depleted W-W/Ni bond (EXAFS fit text, WT, DFT charge) -> d-d decoupling MEC and reaction-path MEC (F4e) -> best M-WO2 activity (F4a) -> eta10 benchmark (F4d) and 100 h stability (F4c) -> conclusion. Audits: a1 (volcano right leg is a broken W-Cu configuration), a2 (Co and Cu share dG_H* but differ by ~80 mV; text-silent). F4 is tier C: no panels offered although crop files exist on disk; F4 cited with panel_ids []. Tafel, Rct, XPS, post-test XRD/SEM (SI figures) kept in image_notes. No multi-cause claims. Judge (C18): n9 and n10 split (n22 anneal optimum, n21 Ni distribution), o22 split (o27 inset LSV), n6 retyped PRP/descriptor.",
 "review": {
  "judge": "senior investigator",
  "verdict": "accept with minor changes",
  "checklist": {
   "spine_primary_argument": "yes: need -> d-d coupling hypothesis -> WO2 base + M sweep -> computed W-M bond weakening (STR) -> dG_H* volcano (PRP/descriptor) -> down-select Ni -> hydrothermal NWs -> reductive anneal -> single-phase Ni-WO2 -> oxidised W -> longer, charge-depleted W-W/Ni bond -> d-d decoupling MEC and reaction-path MEC -> best M-WO2 activity (PRP) -> eta10 benchmark and 100 h stability (PRF) -> conclusion. Computation-first loop (DES -> STR -> PRP -> down_select -> PRC) is allowed by the down_select rule",
   "spine_nodes": 18,
   "spine_connected": true,
   "spine_claims_evidenced": "n5 (o1,o2,o3,k1), n6 (o4,k2; a1 qualifies), n10 (o5,o8; n21 supports), n13 (o10,k3), n14 (o13,o15,o16), n15 (o19; a2 qualifies), n20 (o25,o26), n16 (o18), n17 (o24), n18 (o22,o27)",
